From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000001 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Security Research Team <security-research@upstream.kernel.org>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] sched_ext: Enforce minimum dispatch slice floor for
 protected security tasks

The extensible scheduler class (sched_ext) allows custom BPF struct_ops
schedulers to assign arbitrary execution slices via scx_bpf_dsq_insert()
and scx_bpf_dispatch(). While the sched_ext infrastructure provides a
timeout watchdog (default 5000ms) to detect total task starvation, an
adversarial scheduler can bypass this watchdog entirely by allocating
microsecond-scale time slices (e.g., 50us to 500us) or selectively skipping
dispatch cycles.

Under this adversarial scheduling pattern, security monitoring daemons
(such as EDR agents and audit collectors) are starved below their ingestion
rate while still executing frequently enough to satisfy the 5-second
watchdog, causing kernel ring buffers to overflow and drop telemetry
silently.

This patch introduces a minimum slice floor in scx_bpf_dsq_insert(). For
tasks possessing CAP_SYS_PTRACE or belonging to protected cgroups
(cgroup_is_oom_group or critical security service hierarchies), the
allocated slice is clamped to at least sysctl_sched_min_granularity:

    slice = max_t(u64, slice, sysctl_sched_min_granularity);

This guarantees that protected security tasks receive sufficient quantum
to process buffered kernel telemetry before preemption.

Signed-off-by: Security Research Team <security-research@upstream.kernel.org>
---
 kernel/sched/ext.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel/sched/ext.c b/kernel/sched/ext.c
index 4b9a8f21e8..7c3d1e90a2 100644
--- a/kernel/sched/ext.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/ext.c
@@ -4820,6 +4820,18 @@ static bool scx_task_is_protected(struct task_struct *p)
 {
+	/* Security daemons and tracer tasks holding CAP_SYS_PTRACE */
+	if (has_capability_noaudit(p, CAP_SYS_PTRACE))
+		return true;
+
+	/* Tasks in cgroups marked for group OOM protection or system critical slice */
+#ifdef CONFIG_MEMCG
+	if (mem_cgroup_from_task(p) && mem_cgroup_oom_group_possible(mem_cgroup_from_task(p)))
+		return true;
+#endif
+
+	return false;
 }
 
 /**
  * scx_bpf_dsq_insert - Insert a task into a dispatch queue
  * @p: task_struct to insert
  * @dsq_id: DSQ ID
  * @slice: execution slice in nanoseconds
  * @enq_flags: SCX_ENQ_* flags
  */
 void scx_bpf_dsq_insert(struct task_struct *p, u64 dsq_id, u64 slice, u64 enq_flags)
 {
+	/*
+	 * Starvation mitigation: clamp slice to minimum granularity floor
+	 * for protected monitoring and security tasks to prevent ringbuffer drop attacks.
+	 */
+	if (unlikely(scx_task_is_protected(p))) {
+		u64 min_floor = (u64)sysctl_sched_min_granularity;
+		if (slice < min_floor)
+			slice = min_floor;
+	}
+
 	__scx_bpf_dsq_insert(p, dsq_id, slice, enq_flags);
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(scx_bpf_dsq_insert);
